Description: Provides quantitative methods for empirical research in
    political economy, with applications to food security, household
    economic vulnerability, and inequality. Computes weighted,
    rank-dependent concentration and inequality indices with explicit
    treatment of tied ranks. Supports variance estimation with survey
    replicate weights and recomputes fractional ranks for each replicate.
